--- a/docs/source/changelog.rst
+++ b/docs/source/changelog.rst
@@ -7,6 +7,29 @@
 
 Added
 ^^^^^
+
+- Added separate Wolf soft/hard support-terrain methods tasks with dual reward
+  critics, global/local terrain representation teaching, one-step proprioceptive
+  prediction, and constrained-domain LIPM/CLF-like shaping. These are method
+  adaptations, not full paper reproductions.
+
+- Added matched Wolf method ablation profiles, including an explicit HIM-off
+  mechanism control, a description-only default launcher, and a 2000-iteration
+  minimum for formal methods training.
+
+- Added opt-in Wolf distillation with MSE/Huber, performance-gated DAgger,
+  bounded replay, frozen same-state teacher labels, and fail-closed
+  control-contract qualification.
+
+- Added an opt-in Wolf URDF-speed software guard experiment with frozen-policy
+  comparisons; original task profiles remain unchanged and no state clipping
+  is applied.
+
+- Added source-pinned Wolf design/control contract checks, preserving the
+  current upstream parameters and documenting older policy incompatibilities.
+
+- Added Wolf flat/rough PPO and HIM task configurations from alldog_mjlab;
+  original Wolf STL assets and URDF are included locally.
 
 - Added a ``cu126`` extra (``uv sync --extra cu126``) that installs torch built for
   CUDA 12.6, for machines whose NVIDIA driver is older than 580. It does not include
@@ -26,6 +49,12 @@
 
 Fixed
 ^^^^^
+
+- Reject nonfinite Wolf HIM estimator and policy losses or gradients before
+  their optimizer step instead of writing invalid parameters.
+
+- Restored Wolf HIM critic observation-normalization updates for RSL-RL 5.5
+  and reject unsupported training options before initialization.
 
 - The viewer now resets recurrent policy hidden state for environments that terminate
   or time out. Previously it only reset the policy when the user pressed the reset
